#-----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Vibrational-Translational (VT) relaxation of N2(v)
#
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------
# SSH theory and approximations for the Morse oscillator model.
# M. Capitelli, et al., Plasma Kinetics in Atmospheric Gases, Springer-Verlag, Berlin, Heidelberg, New York, 2000.
# A. Starikovskiy and N. Aleksandrov, Prog. Energy Combust. Sci. 39 (1) (2013) 61-110.
# A. Starikovskiy and N. Aleksandrov, Mechanism of Plasma-Assisted Ignition for H2 and C1-C5 Hydrocarbons, 55th AIAA Aerospace Sciences Meeting, 2017
# The VT relaxation rate constant of N2(v1) with DME is assumed as the same as N2(v1) with C2H6.
N2(v1) + CH3OCH3 => N2 + CH3OCH3          !  kVT10_N2DME
N2(v2) + CH3OCH3 => N2(v1) + CH3OCH3      !  kVT10_N2DME*2.012*exp(2.288d0/Tgas**(1.0d0/3.0d0))
N2(v3) + CH3OCH3 => N2(v2) + CH3OCH3      !  kVT10_N2DME*3.037*exp(4.551d0/Tgas**(1.0d0/3.0d0))
N2(v4) + CH3OCH3 => N2(v3) + CH3OCH3      !  kVT10_N2DME*4.075*exp(6.826d0/Tgas**(1.0d0/3.0d0))
N2(v5) + CH3OCH3 => N2(v4) + CH3OCH3      !  kVT10_N2DME*5.125*exp(9.101d0/Tgas**(1.0d0/3.0d0))
N2(v6) + CH3OCH3 => N2(v5) + CH3OCH3      !  kVT10_N2DME*6.189*exp(11.377d0/Tgas**(1.0d0/3.0d0))
N2(v7) + CH3OCH3 => N2(v6) + CH3OCH3      !  kVT10_N2DME*7.266*exp(13.652d0/Tgas**(1.0d0/3.0d0))
N2(v8) + CH3OCH3 => N2(v7) + CH3OCH3      !  kVT10_N2DME*8.357*exp(15.927d0/Tgas**(1.0d0/3.0d0))

